{{also|Anschreiben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{af|de|an-|schreiben}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʔanʃʁaɪ̯bm̩/|/ˈʔanʃʁaɪ̯bən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-anschreiben.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|aɪ̯bən|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|an.schreiben<schrieb,geschrieben>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[write]] to {{gloss|to [[address]] someone in writing, especially via mail}}
#: {{ux|de|Sie musste ihn mehrmals '''anschreiben''', weil sie keine Antwort erhielt.|She had '''to write to''' him several times, because she did not receive an answer.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[write]] on/up {{gloss|to form letters, words or symbols on a surface, such as a blackboard, in order to communicate}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[charge]] (something to someone's account)
#: {{ux|de|Er läßt schon wieder beim Laden '''anschreiben'''.|He had it '''charged to his account''' again at the store.|lit=He let it be '''written''' again at the store.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to begin to write {{gloss|to produce a mark when used as a writing instrument}}
#: {{ux|de|Ein hochwertiger Füller sollte sofort '''anschreiben'''.|A high-quality fountain-pen should '''write''' immediately.}}

